{#
  Renders the message reported when Traefik verification fails, or nothing if it passed.
#}
{% set pod_selector = traefik_pod_selector.items() | map('join', '=') | join(',') %}
{% set probe_status_codes = traefik_verify_probe_status_codes | map('string') | list %}
{% set api_failures = traefik_verify_api.results | rejectattr('rc', 'equalto', 0) | list %}
{% set bad_probes = traefik_verify_probes.results | rejectattr('stdout', 'in', probe_status_codes) | list %}
{% if not traefik_verify_pods.stdout or api_failures or traefik_verify_disabled or bad_probes %}
Traefik verification failed. {{ traefik_verify_context | default('') }}
{% if not traefik_verify_pods.stdout %}

No running Traefik pods were found in namespace {{ traefik_release_namespace }}.
Check the pods with:
  kubectl get pods -n {{ traefik_release_namespace }} -l {{ pod_selector }}
{% endif %}
{# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
{% if api_failures %}

The Traefik API could not be queried on these pods:
{% for result in api_failures %}
  - {{ result.item | join(' ') }}
{% endfor %}
Check that the pods are healthy and that the API is enabled (api.insecure), e.g. with:
  kubectl logs -n {{ traefik_release_namespace }} {{ api_failures[0].item[0] }}
{% endif %}
{# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
{% if traefik_verify_disabled %}

Traefik cannot serve these routers and middlewares:
{% for item in traefik_verify_disabled | sort(attribute = 'name') %}
  {{ item.name }}:
{% for error in item.error | default([item.status | default('disabled')], true) %}
    - {{ error }}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}

These Ingresses use ingress-nginx features that Traefik does not support, such as nginx
configuration snippets.

Upgrade the components that create them to versions that support Traefik by deploying
with ingress_controller_migration_phase set to nginx,
then deploy with it set to traefik again.
{% endif %}
{# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
{% if bad_probes %}

These URLs did not return an expected status ({{ probe_status_codes | join(', ') }}) through the Service {{ traefik_release_namespace }}/{{ traefik_verify_service_name }}:
{% for result in bad_probes %}
  - {{ result.item }} returned {{ result.stdout }}
{% endfor %}
000 means the connection failed, and 404 means Traefik has no route for the URL.
Check the Ingress for the host and the Traefik logs.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
